WEBVTT

00:00.140 --> 00:02.140
It starts with an idea.

00:02.720 --> 00:03.634
Need evidence?

00:03.805 --> 00:06.549
Bellows can trace a claim
back to its source.

00:08.390 --> 00:10.470
Let Harness choose the agent,

00:10.670 --> 00:13.110
model, and effort for each task.

00:13.230 --> 00:14.710
Or set them yourself.

00:17.555 --> 00:21.075
With Anvil, a complex brief
becomes a plan.

00:24.900 --> 00:26.820
Approve it to create the issues.

00:27.684 --> 00:29.844
Forge works through those issues,

00:32.374 --> 00:35.334
runs the tests,
and keeps the results together.

00:38.895 --> 00:41.216
Temper takes it into a real browser,

00:41.339 --> 00:43.206
with a screenshot at each step.

00:46.170 --> 00:50.110
Now you can review the pull request
and see exactly what changed.

00:50.700 --> 00:54.105
Once you approve, Rivet deploys
and checks the release.

00:56.270 --> 00:56.910
Forge.

00:57.370 --> 00:59.850
From idea to working solution.
